Z||000000||Formula||03-24-2000||12:55 PM||||Im going to do a rebody of my formula into a GT in the summer.<P>I plan on buying the turbo window vents, mecham scoops and wheels. then paint it all red and put viper style white stripes on it.<P>I was wondering if anyone has did the front nose, the rear clip, the ground effects, or put a GT style (not the small 84 ones) factory sun roof on a fiero?<P>should I do this or drop a 3.4 TDC in it?<p>[This message has been edited by Formula (edited 03-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||03-24-2000||01:12 PM||||What you are proposing to do is nothing new. Many a notch back has been turned into a fastback. Just need the necessary parts. I turned my 85 GT almost into a Formula. It kinda got stuck in the middle but its kinda neat. Nobody really knows what year it is! Just check out a GT and take notice of the different parts like the wheel wells etc and you should do fine. Sure would love to see the finished product!<P>And why not do both! It would be up to you which to do first. But you may want to put the engine in before the paintjob. You never know what can happen in a shop!<P>Check out Tom's site. 88Formula has already done your conversion from Formula to GT! Its the yellow and black one on the bottom.<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 03-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||03-24-2000||06:44 PM||||I don't have an '84, but what do you mean when you talk about a large GT sunroof?  I was under the assumtion that a Vista Vent is a Vista Vent.  I have an '86 2m4 and an '85 GT and both of the sunroofs are identical.  I have an acquaintance with 2 GTs ('86 and '87) and his sunroofs are the same as mine, too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||03-24-2000||06:51 PM||||As far as I know all of the sunroofs are the same. The hard part is taking the roof off of one Fiero to put it on the other. The "arms" the parts the go down the side of the windshield tend to crack if not taken out with care and a truckload of patience.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||03-24-2000||07:48 PM||||All factory sunroofs were the same dimensions but there were some dealer installed sunroofs that were pretty dinky.  That's likely what he meant by the "small '84 ones".||||reg||1
